        <OtherAbstract Type="Publisher" Language="rus">
            <AbstractText>Izuchena tkanespetsifichnaia ékspressiia genov transporterov kholesterina ABCA1 i ABCG1, a takzhe genov, kodiruiushchikh naibolee vazhnye transkriptsionnye reguliatory adipogeneza – LXRa, LXRb, PPARg i RORa, v intraabdominal'noĭ zhirovoĭ tkani (IZhT) u lits bez izbytochnogo vesa i lits s ozhireniem. Pokazana priamaia korreliatsiia soderzhaniia belkov ABCA1 i ABCG1 v IZhT s urovnem belka RORa (r=0,480, p&lt;0,05; r=0,435, p&lt;0,05 sootvetstvenno), chto pozvoliaet predpolozhit' uchastie transkriptsionnogo faktora RORa v reguliatsii urovnia belkov ABCA1 i ABCG1 v IZhT. Pri étom ékspressiia genov ABCA1 i ABCG1 polozhitel'no korreliruet s takimi pokazateliami, kak indeks massy tela (IMT) (r=0,522, p=0,004; r=0,594, p=0,001 sootvetstvenno) i obkhvat talii (OT) (r=0,403, p=0,033; r=0,474, p=0,013 sootvetstvenno). Razvitie ozhireniia takzhe assotsiirovano so snizheniem urovnia mRNK RORa i LXRb (p=0,016 i p=0,002 sootvetstvenno) v IZhT. Predpolagaetsia, chto iadernyĭ faktor RORa mozhet igrat' znachimuiu rol' v reguliatsii obmena kholesterina i kontrole ékspressii genov ABCA1 i ABCG1 v IZhT, a uroven' ékspressii gena LXRb v IZhT mozhet byt' vazhnym faktorom, assotsiirovannym s razvitiem ozhireniia.</AbstractText>
        </OtherAbstract>
